            <ArticleTitle>Safe coronary artery occlusion with a new tourniquet in off-pump bypass grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery occlusion during off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting may lead to mechanical trauma of the arterial wall. My colleagues and I describe a safe coronary artery occlusion technique in off-pump bypass grafting that uses a new spring-equipped tourniquet, which enables precise adjustment of the least force necessary to occlude the coronary flow. This prevents snare-induced vessel wall damage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
